    "expectedRule": "Void Citadel records the opening style (force=attack, art, guard) of the first offensive action of every non-boss combat victory. Before the boss is engaged, the law shows a preview of the style that would be countered. When the boss combat starts, the assessment is locked: bossAssessmentLocked becomes true and bossCounter is frozen from the non-boss opening distribution, excluding the boss's own placeholder opening record. A distribution is balanced only when all three styles have at least one victory and the max-min spread is at most 1; a balanced distribution locks bossCounter=null and closes the counter, while an imbalanced distribution locks the most-used style (fixed force->art->guard tie order) and applies a -20% penalty to that style's outgoing damage or guard effect for the whole boss encounter. Once locked, the boss's own opening and later hub/top-level state changes cannot backfill the assessment: the player's real opening action in the boss fight does not overwrite the placeholder record, hub commands are refused during combat, and the locked law state survives a save-codec round-trip. Route gates citadel_force_identity_lane, citadel_art_growth_lane, and citadel_guard_echo_lane open after at least one victory with their respective style; citadel_balanced_core_lane opens only for a balanced distribution. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
